n a month after moving in. I got a cold and needed soup. A neighbor recommended this place and I was not disappointed. Good hot & sour soup. More mushrooms/veggies in there than in a lot of places' hot & sour soup, and it had a decent level of spiciness. Usually I get a massive MSG reaction, and I was expecting to have one this time, but in fact there thankfully was none. When I went in to pick it up, they were finishing it and I saw them actually stirring ingredients in and cracking eggs into the broth, so it;s not a massive pre-made batch of glop like you..."},{"business_id":"G5Eq92IZ-GRWFGnUdLQvsw","review_id":"cYZX-_7bzGxSbmEsognOOw","date":"2013-12-19T02:56:20","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9249038100242615,"text_excerpt":"Sucks that they don't deliver. However being from NYC this is the closest to Chinatown Chinese food I've had shofar down in New Orleans. Their steamed dumplings were delicious as well as their general tso's chicken...also they take credit cards! I know where to go now when I'm drunk, hungover or lazy and need a superior dose of high quality msg!"},{"business_id":"G5Eq92IZ-GRWFGnUdLQvsw","review_id":"MtiYz9rlLxsorc3ExEtpUA","date":"2018-09-21T19:13:46","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9029688835144043,"text_excerpt":"I'm from NYC and Chinese from anywhere else is just subpar compared to there but this Chinese restaurant shocked me ! Little hole in the wall but the food is really yummy ! Especially the hot and sour soup ! I think one of the best Chinese spots in New Orleans to be honest !"}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
